AIAQ Knowledge Intelligence System
Local-first knowledge retrieval, project context recovery, and evidence-assisted engineering decisions.

AIAQ Knowledge Intelligence System (KIS) is an internal, production-oriented AI knowledge layer developed by AIAQ Lab for its self-hosted AI Hub. It helps recover relevant information from approved project materials, return to ongoing engineering work with better context, and prepare source-grounded evidence for technical review.

Rather than creating another general-purpose chatbot or duplicating existing infrastructure, KIS connects selected knowledge sources through a controlled retrieval workflow. The original documents and repositories remain the sources of truth.
Public showcase: This repository provides a high-level project case study. The working implementation, private knowledge base, source documents, internal architecture, security configuration, prompts, infrastructure details, credentials, and commercially sensitive materials are not published.

What It Solves
Operating multiple AI and automation projects creates recurring knowledge-management problems:
- Decisions, technical findings, and project history are scattered across documents and repositories.
- Returning to a paused project requires time-consuming manual reconstruction of its current state.
- Exact identifiers, errors, revisions, and test evidence can be difficult to locate.
- Semantic search alone can miss critical filenames, requirement IDs, or version-specific facts.
- Old reports may be mistaken for current system status.
- AI-generated explanations can be confused with verified engineering evidence.
- Rebuilding the same context repeatedly slows down development and delivery.
KIS addresses these problems with source-aware search, bounded context recovery, and evidence-first review.
